 **Discretization and Compositing Steps:**
 The integral is approximated by dividing the ray into $n$ equal segments [S2, S3, unofficial]. The standard iterative approach uses front-to-back alpha compositing [S3, unofficial]:
-1.  Initialize accumulated color $C_{acc} = 0$ and accumulated opacity $\alpha_{acc} = 0$ [S3, unofficial].
-2.  For each segment $i$ from $0$ to $n-1$:
-    a. Evaluate extinction $k_i = k(s_0 + i\Delta t)$ and emission $q_i = q(s_0 + i\Delta t)$ [S2, S3, unofficial].
-    b. Calculate segment transmittance $T_i = e^{-k_i \Delta t}$ [S2, S3, unofficial].
-    c. Calculate segment opacity $\alpha_i = 1 - T_i$ [S3, unofficial, S4].
-    d. Calculate segment pre-multiplied color $\hat{C}_i = q_i \Delta t \cdot \alpha_i$ [S3, unofficial].
-    e. Update accumulators: $\alpha_{acc} = \alpha_{acc} + (1 - \alpha_{acc}) \alpha_i$ and $C_{acc} = C_{acc} + (1 - \alpha_{acc}) \hat{C}_i$ [S3, unofficial].
-3.  Composite the background: $I(D) = C_{acc} + I_0 (1 - \alpha_{acc})$ [S2, S4].
